From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:19:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-cheetah: enable the GPU

Enable the Mali-G710 on the Pixel 7 Pro. Panthor is built as a module;
during bring-up userspace keeps it from autoloading and loads it by
hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
index fbb8195db..29b0330f0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
@@ -76,6 +76,11 @@ cont_splash_mem: splash@fac00000 {
 	};
 };
 
+&gpu {
+	/* No mali-supply: the G3D rails follow the PMU power domain and ACPM. */
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /* Touchscreen: Synaptics S3908 on USI0 SPI */
 &usi0 {
 	samsung,mode = <USI_MODE_SPI>;
